# Log captures and one-off drops
logs-snapshot/
*.log
# ...except the committed test evidence. Each report under this directory names
# the stdout it was assembled from, in a `stdout:` header, and is rebuilt from
# those bytes by assemble-evidence.py. A report naming a log the repository does
# not carry is exactly the defect that rule exists to stop: a number nobody on a
# fresh clone can re-derive (#302). These captures are produced by the committed
# instruments beside them, print repository-relative paths only, and carry no
# connection string.
#
# PER PRODUCER, NOT `*.log`. The negation used to re-include every `.log` that
# landed in this directory, produced or not, which is a rule that cannot refuse
# anything (#342): a file nothing in this tree writes was admitted by the same
# line as a capture, and an `add -A` over a working directory would carry it.
# Each pattern below is the capture of ONE committed instrument beside it, and
# the name it is paired against is a VALUE that instrument produces rather
# than a sentence written beside it. Seven of the eight are redirected into
# their capture by their caller and print its name in their own stdout header.
# The eighth, repin-last.py, OPENS its capture itself: one function decides
# that name, the wrapper writes the same value into the log's own header, and
# it REFUSES to run when the name it is about to write is not re-included
# below. So the set stays derivable rather than remembered, and a producer
# whose capture this block cannot carry stops before the run instead of at the
# `git add` after it.
# test_the_evidence_log_negation_admits_only_produced_logs compares the two
# sets in BOTH directions: a pattern no instrument produces reds, and a capture
# an instrument names that no pattern admits reds.
#
# ROUND 13: EXACT NAMES, NOT SUFFIX WILDCARDS. The per-producer patterns were
# `*-suite-run.log` and seven siblings, which is narrower than `*.log` and
# still admits any file that lands here with a producer's SUFFIX -- a name no
# instrument in this tree writes, under a round that does not exist, carried
# into an `add -A` by the same line as the evidence. A negation is a promise
# that the repository carries this file on purpose, so each line below is the
# whole name of ONE capture of ONE round: the producer's own suffix, behind
# the round it belongs to. Nothing here is a pattern, so nothing here can
# admit a name nobody produced.
#
# The suffixes are still DERIVED rather than remembered. Every instrument
# beside this directory names the capture it writes -- seven print it in their
# stdout header because a caller redirects them into it, and repin-last.py
# returns it from `capture_name()` because it opens the file itself -- and the
# check reads the suffix off the instrument and the round off this list. A
# round that adds a capture and not its line refuses before the run: the
# wrapper asks `capture_is_admitted()` first, and the both-directions test
# requires the NEWEST round's line to exist for every producer.
#
# round 10
!backend/tests/evidence/r10-suite-run.log
!backend/tests/evidence/r10-pg-controls.log
!backend/tests/evidence/r10-mutation-run.log
!backend/tests/evidence/r10-citation-pin.log
!backend/tests/evidence/r10-freeze-guard.log
!backend/tests/evidence/r10-repin-run.log
!backend/tests/evidence/r10-suites-assembly-run.log
# round 11
!backend/tests/evidence/r11-suite-run.log
!backend/tests/evidence/r11-pg-controls.log
!backend/tests/evidence/r11-mutation-run.log
!backend/tests/evidence/r11-citation-pin.log
!backend/tests/evidence/r11-freeze-guard.log
!backend/tests/evidence/r11-repin-run.log
!backend/tests/evidence/r11-suites-assembly-run.log
